# 0804 — SERIES 800 PATENT IDEAS

## LEGAiSEE COMMANDCENTER KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM

Version: 1.0
Status: ACTIVE GOVERNANCE STANDARD

---

# PURPOSE

The Patent Ideas subsystem captures novel, potentially protectable intellectual property generated through research, experimentation, and system evolution within the LEGAiSEE CommandCenter.

This subsystem exists to formalize invention tracking, structure originality, and preserve intellectual artifacts that may have legal, commercial, or strategic value.

Patent Ideas are not production features.

They are structured invention candidates.

---

# CORE PRINCIPLE

Innovation has value before implementation.

The system must preserve and structure novelty at the moment it emerges, not after it becomes embedded in production systems.

Patent Ideas ensure that originality is not lost inside operational execution.

---

# OBJECTIVES

The Patent Ideas subsystem shall:

* capture novel system inventions
* structure intellectual property concepts
* preserve original design intent
* document inventive mechanisms
* support commercialization pathways
* enable legal review readiness
* track invention evolution
* prevent loss of intellectual novelty

---

# PATENT IDEA SCOPE

Patent Ideas may include:

* new AI reasoning architectures
* novel graph intelligence systems
* unique orchestration mechanisms
* adaptive workflow engines
* memory augmentation systems
* predictive intelligence methods
* interface interaction paradigms
* data transformation techniques
* automation frameworks

Any non-trivial system innovation may qualify.

---

# IDEA CLASSIFICATION

Patent Ideas are categorized by maturity and structure.

---

## Conceptual Invention

Early-stage idea without implementation.

* theoretical model
* architectural proposal
* abstract mechanism
* system hypothesis

---

## Prototype-Backed Invention

Idea supported by experimental validation.

* derived from Series 802 experiments
* partially implemented systems
* measurable behavior observed

---

## System-Integrated Invention

Innovation already present in system design but not yet formally recognized.

* embedded architecture patterns
* emergent system behavior
* undocumented mechanisms

---

## Commercially Viable Invention

Ideas suitable for external protection and commercialization.

* clearly defined mechanism
* differentiated innovation
* potential market application
* legal defensibility potential

---

# PATENT IDEA STRUCTURE

Each invention record shall include:

* invention title
* system domain
* problem statement
* proposed mechanism
* novelty description
* comparative advantage
* supporting evidence
* experimental references (if any)
* implementation potential
* risk considerations

Structure ensures legal and technical clarity.

---

